    "topFinding": "Two of this run's HIGH findings are real, live user-facing exposure, not process debt: a corrupted localStorage entry now silently discards a user's autosaved label or their entire saved-label library with zero on-screen warning (reliability-01), and three modules still double-instantiate on every page load through the same static-import pattern that caused the v0.11.0 blank-page outage, with 4 of 7 edges fixed in v1.1.7 but 3 left open (architecture-01). Separately, the WCAG contrast fix that v1.1.6/v1.1.7 described as finished was checked against the wrong bar: it targeted 3:1 when the actual text falls under the 4.5:1 threshold, so 127 of 199 herb accent colors still fail contrast, including the three families the changelog called finished (generative-art-palette-discipline-01, now HIGH). Against that, real ground moved: the chronic 43-record mid-word truncation bug is genuinely fixed, the dashboard stale-flag gap closed, and the per-project script stack rewrite landed clean. Orchestration debt is largely the same shared-portfolio picture as Scheduler's review today: queue-drain-hourly still disabled, the plugin republish still pending, the skill-trigger reciprocal clause still missing everywhere.",
